/* book Worked example: Q: A three-phase fully controlled bridge runs from a 400 V, 50 Hz line with a source inductance of 1 mH per phase and a level load current of 20 A. Find ωLs, ΔVd, the output at α = 0 and the overlap angle at α = 0 and at α = 60°.
   1. ω = 2π × 50 = 314.16 rad/s; ωLs = 314.16 × 0.001 = 0.3142 Ω.
   2. ΔVd = 3ωLs Id/π = 3 × 0.3142 × 20/π = 6.00 V.
   3. Vd0 = 3√2 × 400/π = 540.19 V, so at α = 0 Vdc = 540.19 − 6.00 = 534.19 V.
   4. 2ωLs Id/(√2 VL) = 2 × 0.3142 × 20/565.69 = 0.0222. At α = 0: cos μ = 1 − 0.0222 = 0.9778, μ = 12.1°.
   5. At α = 60°: cos(60° + μ) = 0.5 − 0.0222 = 0.4778, so 60° + μ = 61.46° and μ = 1.46°. The same current overlaps far less near 90°.
   Answer: ωLs = 0.314 Ω, ΔVd = 6.0 V, Vdc(α = 0) = 534.2 V, μ = 12.1° at α = 0 and 1.46° at α = 60°. */
