/* book Worked example 2: Q: A single-phase fully controlled bridge on 230 V, 50 Hz has a total source inductance Ls = 5 mH and carries a level 20 A at α = 30°. Find μ, ΔVd and Vdc.
   1. Vm = 325.27 V; ωLs = 314.16 × 0.005 = 1.571 Ω.
   2. cos(α + μ) = cos 30° − 2ωLs Id/Vm = 0.8660 − (2 × 1.571 × 20)/325.27 = 0.8660 − 0.1932 = 0.6729, so α + μ = 47.71° and μ = 17.71°.
   3. ΔVd = 2ωLs Id/π = 2 × 1.571 × 20/π = 20.0 V.
   4. Vdc = 207.07 × 0.8660 − 20.0 = 179.33 − 20.0 = 159.33 V.
   5. Check with the second form: (Vm/π)[cos α + cos(α + μ)] = 103.54 × (0.8660 + 0.6729) = 159.33 V.
   Answer: μ = 17.7°, ΔVd = 20.0 V, Vdc = 159.3 V instead of 179.3 V without Ls. */
