/* book exam traps: Blaming the DC smoothing choke for the overlap. Only inductance on the AC side delays the transfer of current. | Forgetting the drop at α = 0. ΔVd is subtracted after the cosine term, so even full output loses it. | Using 3ωLs Id/π for a single-phase bridge. It is 2ωLs Id/π there; 3 belongs to the six-pulse bridge. | Putting the phase voltage or the peak into the three-phase overlap formula. It needs √2 VL, the line peak. | Calling Rc a real resistor. It wastes no power; it only models the lost volt-seconds. */
