/* book Worked example 2: Q: A three-phase bridge on 400 V, 50 Hz with Ls = 1 mH per phase works as an inverter with a minimum extinction angle γ0 = 15°. Find α_max, μ and Vdc at Id = 100 A, and α_max at Id = 20 A.
   1. Vd0 = 540.19 V; ωLs = 0.3142 Ω.
   2. At 100 A: 2ωLs Id/(√2 VL) = 2 × 0.3142 × 100/565.69 = 0.1111. cos α_max = 0.1111 − cos 15° = 0.1111 − 0.9659 = −0.8549, so α_max = 148.7°.
   3. μ = 180° − 15° − 148.7° = 16.3°.
   4. ΔVd = 3 × 0.3142 × 100/π = 30.0 V. Vdc = 540.19 × cos 148.7° − 30.0 = −461.8 − 30.0 = −491.8 V. Check: (Vd0/2)(cos α − cos γ) = 270.09 × (−0.8549 − 0.9659) = −491.8 V.
   5. Power returned = 491.8 × 100 = 49.2 kW.
   6. At 20 A: 2ωLs Id/(√2 VL) = 0.0222, cos α_max = 0.0222 − 0.9659 = −0.9437, α_max = 160.7° (μ = 4.3°).
   Answer: At 100 A: α_max = 148.7°, μ = 16.3°, Vdc = −491.8 V (49.2 kW returned). At 20 A the limit rises to 160.7°. */
